 "en": {
  "intro": "Based on the role of the Agricultural Pesticides Committee as stated in Agriculture Law No. 53 of 1966 and the regulating ministerial decisions, the latest being Ministerial Decision No. 974 of 2017, the Committee strives to cover all Egyptian crops with technical recommendations for agricultural pesticides in order to control agricultural pests in all their forms, stressing the safe and effective use of pesticides so that clean food reaches the Egyptian citizen, the Egyptian environment is protected, and the reputation of Egyptian agricultural exports abroad is preserved. On that basis, the Committee reviewed all crops and the economic pests that attack them, together with the pesticide recommendations available to it for their control. It emerged that a number of crops grown in Egypt have no recommendations at all for the pests that affect them. These are the crops termed “Minor Crops”, meaning areas of less than 50,000 feddan. The Committee considers it necessary and important to have recommendations for them, to complete the pest-management system in Egypt. What follows lists these crops and the area planted with each in Egypt, together with examples of pesticides that may be considered for trials ahead of recommending them. So that approved recommendations exist for all crops, the crops in each item (table) below may be treated as a crop group, so that a pesticide is recommended if it passes the registration limits for the crop group rather than for a single crop.",
